import numpy as np

DESCRIPTION = ("Mechanism: h0=0; h_t = relu(x_t*Wx + h_{t-1}@Wh), out = h8@Wo, decision = argmax class score. Written in the hidden-unit gauge that makes the input "
               "weights exactly +-1 (WXP below), so the 8 input weights cost no constants; the readout is applied in the difference (class-shift) basis, "
               "score_j - score_0, which also costs no constants. The recurrent matrix and the readout are generic trained weights, given exactly. "
               "The relus are active in almost every unit at every step, so the state propagates the 8 inputs multiplicatively through 7 recurrent steps "
               "(|h8| ~ 19, growing); class scores are near ties which makes the decision depend on every weight.")

