import numpy as np

DESCRIPTION = ("Mechanism. Step 1: h1 = |x1| * one-hot(sign(x1)) per unit, i.e. each unit starts as the positive or negative part of the first input "
               "(the input weights are pure signs - the gauge is chosen so they are exactly +-1, which is why they cost no constants). "
               "Steps 2-8: h_t = relu(h_{t-1}@Wh + x_t*signs); the recurrent matrix has complex-conjugate eigenvalue pairs (a damping/oscillatory "
               "mixture), the relus are active in almost every unit at almost every step, and the state grows multiplicatively (mean |h8| ~ 19, "
               "max 148): so the network propagates the 8 inputs through 7 recurrent steps and reads off 8 class scores. The decision is argmax_j "
               "(s_j - s_0) over the 7 score differences of the last state, i.e. a comparison of 8 oscillatory projections of the input history. "
               "Every recurrent weight and every readout entry matters and matters at the 1e-4 level: the class scores are near ties (margin 0.44 "
               "on a score scale of 6.6), so there is no threshold/count/max rule with fewer numbers - the 119 constants below are one per degree of "
               "freedom of the network (136 weights less the 8 hidden-unit scales and the 8 class-score shifts and 1 overall scale that leave its "
               "decisions unchanged), i.e. this is the maximally compressed exact description of the network.")

